---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Omit the Tumtum — Daf Yomi Game: Bekhorot 42"
  description="Bekhorot 42: take the Gemara's red pen to six baraitot (סמי מכאן טומטום), refill Rabbi Elazar's list of five, test where a tumtum animal urinates, and trace the tumtum through betrothal and ḥalitza."
>
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Frank+Ruhl+Libre:wght@300;400;700;900&display=swap" />

  <style is:global>
    .frank { font-family: 'Frank Ruhl Libre', serif; }
    .card { background: #11131b; border: 1px solid #262a3a; border-radius: 1rem; }
    .chip { border: 1px solid #3a3f55; border-radius: 0.6rem; padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem; font-size: 0.8rem; transition: background .15s, border-color .15s; text-align: left; }
    .chip:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #191c28; }
    .chip.ok { background: #13261f; border-color: #6cc3a6; }
    .chip.bad { background: #33191a; border-color: #cc5a48; }
    .chip:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: .92; }
    .tgl { border: 1px solid #3a3f55; border-radius: 999px; padding: .35rem .9rem; font-size: .8rem; }
    .tgl[aria-pressed="true"] { background: #2a2414; border-color: #e0b54a; }
    .lamp { display: inline-block; width: .7rem; height: .7rem; border-radius: 999px; background: #3a3f55; margin-right: .35rem; }
    .lamp.g { background: #6cc3a6; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #6cc3a6; }
    .lamp.r { background: #cc5a48; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #cc5a48; }
    .lamp.y { background: #e0b54a; box-shadow: 0 0 8px #e0b54a; }
    .quote { background: #0d0f16; border-inline-start: 3px solid #3a3f55; padding: .6rem .85rem; border-radius: .4rem; font-size: .9rem; line-height: 1.6; }
    .w { border-bottom: 2px dotted #e0b54a; padding: 0 .1rem; }
    .w.struck { text-decoration: line-through; text-decoration-color: #cc5a48; text-decoration-thickness: 3px; opacity: .55; border-bottom: 0; transition: opacity .4s; }
    .stream { transition: opacity .3s; }
    button:focus-visible, [tabindex]:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid #e0b54a; outline-offset: 2px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .chip, .w.struck, .stream { transition: none; } }
  </style>

  <main class="min-h-screen bg-[#0a0b10] !text-[#e7e9f0]">

    <div class="border-b border-[#262a3a] bg-gradient-to-b from-[#161a2a] to-transparent px-4 pt-10 pb-8 text-center">
      <p class="mb-3 text-xs tracking-[0.22em] !text-[#959bb3]">
        <a href="/daf" class="transition-colors hover:!text-[#e7e9f0]">daf yomi arcade</a>
        <span class="mx-2 opacity-40">·</span>bekhorot 42<span class="mx-2 opacity-40">·</span>2026-10-30
      </p>
      <div class="mx-auto mb-3 text-5xl" aria-hidden="true">🖍️</div>
      <h1 class="frank text-4xl font-black tracking-tight sm:text-5xl !text-[#f4f5fa]">Omit the Tumtum</h1>
      <p class="frank mt-3 text-3xl font-light !text-[#e0b54a]" dir="rtl" lang="he">סְמִי מִיכָּן טוּמְטוּם</p>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-sm leading-relaxed !text-[#adb2c7]">
        Six times the Gemara says "strike the tumtum from this baraita," and once it can't. Take the red pen, fix a list that comes up one short,
        test where an animal urinates, and follow the tumtum through betrothal and ḥalitza.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs !text-[#959bb3]">Score: <span id="score" class="font-bold !text-[#e0b54a]">0</span> / <span id="max" class="font-bold !text-[#e0b54a]">0</span></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-6 px-4 py-8">

      <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="h1r">
        <h2 id="h1r" class="frank mb-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">1 · The red pen</h2>
        <p class="mb-4 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">Rabbi Yoḥanan's question is whether a <em>tumtum</em> (genitals concealed) is a person of <em>doubtful</em> sex or a third kind of creature, like a hermaphrodite. Each baraita seems to treat it as a third kind. The Gemara's fix is to cross out the word. For each baraita, what does the Gemara do? <span id="penNote"></span></p>
        <div id="pen" class="flex flex-col gap-5"></div>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="h2r">
        <h2 id="h2r" class="frank mb-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">2 · Five animals, now four</h2>
        <p class="mb-3 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">Rabbi Elazar's baraita says <strong>five</strong> animals are neither consecrated nor make others consecrated <a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42a.10" target="_blank" rel="noopener">(42a:10)</a>. Tap the tumtum to strike it, then see the count.</p>
        <div id="five" class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2"></div>
        <p class="mb-2 text-sm"><span id="fiveCount" class="font-bold !text-[#e0b54a]">5 listed</span>. <span id="fiveAsk" class="!text-[#adb2c7]">Strike the tumtum.</span></p>
        <div id="fiveFix" class="grid gap-2"></div>
        <p id="fiveMsg" class="mt-3 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="h3r">
        <h2 id="h3r" class="frank mb-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">3 · Where does it urinate?</h2>
        <p class="mb-3 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">A firstborn animal with concealed genitals. Rabbi Elazar rules by where it urinates, and the Gemara says that only follows one Sage <a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42b.2" target="_blank" rel="noopener">(42b:2)</a>. Set the three controls and read the lamp.</p>
        <div class="mb-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Species">
          <button id="spA" class="tgl" aria-pressed="true">🐑 Animal</button>
          <button id="spP" class="tgl" aria-pressed="false">🧍 Person</button>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-2 flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Where it urinates">
          <button id="plM" class="tgl" aria-pressed="true">💧 from the male place</button>
          <button id="plF" class="tgl" aria-pressed="false">💧 from the female place</button>
        </div>
        <div class="mb-4 flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Sage">
          <button id="sgR" class="tgl" aria-pressed="true">The Rabbis</button>
          <button id="sgS" class="tgl" aria-pressed="false">R. Shimon ben Yehuda</button>
        </div>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 320 120" class="mb-3 w-full max-w-sm" role="img" aria-label="Animal diagram with two possible urination points">
          <ellipse cx="150" cy="55" rx="85" ry="32" fill="#2a2e40" stroke="#3a3f55" />
          <circle cx="245" cy="40" r="20" fill="#2a2e40" stroke="#3a3f55" />
          <rect x="95" y="82" width="8" height="26" fill="#3a3f55" /><rect x="185" y="82" width="8" height="26" fill="#3a3f55" />
          <circle cx="170" cy="82" r="5" fill="#59a0d8" /><text x="170" y="75" font-size="9" fill="#adb2c7" text-anchor="middle">male place</text>
          <circle cx="120" cy="84" r="5" fill="#d86fa0" /><text x="120" y="96" font-size="9" fill="#adb2c7" text-anchor="middle">female place</text>
          <g id="strM" class="stream"><line x1="170" y1="88" x2="170" y2="116" stroke="#e0b54a" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="4 3" /></g>
          <g id="strF" class="stream" opacity="0"><line x1="120" y1="90" x2="120" y2="116" stroke="#e0b54a" stroke-width="3" stroke-dasharray="4 3" /></g>
        </svg>
        <p class="text-sm"><span id="uLamp" class="lamp"></span><strong id="uRes"></strong></p>
        <p id="uWhy" class="mt-1 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]"></p>
        <h3 class="frank mb-2 mt-5 text-lg font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">Why would the Rabbis still worry?</h3>
        <div id="chg" class="grid gap-2"></div>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="h4r">
        <h2 id="h4r" class="frank mb-1 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">4 · The tumtum in marriage</h2>
        <p class="mb-3 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">The baraitot on betrothal and ḥalitza <a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42b.8" target="_blank" rel="noopener">(42b:8-9)</a>. Because "since it changed, it changed" applies to everyone here, the two baraitot split on something else. Flip the switch for the dispute that explains them <a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42b.13" target="_blank" rel="noopener">(42b:13)</a>.</p>
        <div class="mb-3 flex flex-wrap gap-2" role="group" aria-label="Rabbi Eliezer or Rabbi Akiva">
          <button id="eEl" class="tgl" aria-pressed="true">Rabbi Eliezer</button>
          <button id="eAk" class="tgl" aria-pressed="false">Rabbi Akiva</button>
        </div>
        <p class="mb-1 text-sm"><span id="eLamp" class="lamp"></span><span id="eRule"></span></p>
        <p class="mb-4 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">Therefore: <strong id="eBar"></strong></p>
        <div id="marry" class="flex flex-col gap-4"></div>
        <p class="mt-5 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">The Gemara ends the amud with Rabbi Yehuda against Rabbi Yosei son of Rabbi Yehuda on a tumtum who was torn open and found male <a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42b.15" target="_blank" rel="noopener">(42b:15-18)</a>, then asks Rava what practical difference remains. The answer is on the next daf.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="card p-5" aria-labelledby="hl">
        <h2 id="hl" class="frank mb-2 text-2xl font-bold !text-[#f4f5fa]">Learn the real daf</h2>
        <p class="mb-3 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]">The game only samples it. Read the whole page on Sefaria:</p>
        <ul class="mb-3 list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm">
          <li><a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bekhorot 42a</a> · <a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Bekhorot.42b" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bekhorot 42b</a></li>
          <li><a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.42a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rashi on Bekhorot 42a</a> (the most-linked commentary on this daf)</li>
          <li><a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rashi_on_Bekhorot.42b" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rashi on Bekhorot 42b</a></li>
          <li><a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" href="https://www.sefaria.org/Rabbeinu_Gershom_on_Bekhorot.42a" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Rabbeinu Gershom on Bekhorot 42a</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-xs !text-[#959bb3]">Simplified for play. The daf has more cases than the game shows. <a href="/daf" class="underline">All daf games</a></p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>

  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      var $ = function (id) { return document.getElementById(id); };
      var score = 0, max = 0;
      function addMax(n) { max += n; $('max').textContent = max; }
      function award() { score++; $('score').textContent = score; }
      function sef(r) { return '<a class="underline !text-[#e0b54a]" target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.sefaria.org/' + r.replace(/ /g, '_').replace(/:/g, '.') + '">(' + r + ')</a>'; }
      function mkChip(txt, cls) { var b = document.createElement('button'); b.className = 'chip ' + (cls || ''); b.textContent = txt; return b; }
      function mc(box, opts, onDone) {
        var done = false;
        opts.forEach(function (o) {
          var b = mkChip(o.t);
          b.addEventListener('click', function () {
            if (done) return; done = true;
            Array.prototype.forEach.call(box.children, function (c, i) { c.disabled = true; if (opts[i].ok) c.classList.add('ok'); });
            if (!o.ok) b.classList.add('bad');
            onDone(!!o.ok);
          });
          box.appendChild(b);
        });
      }

      // ROUND 1: red pen
      var pen = [
        { ref: '42a:1', q: 'Why then does the baraita on the valuation of Leviticus 27:3 say "the male": <span class="w">a definite male</span>, but <span class="w">not a tumtum</span> and <span class="w">hermaphrodite</span>?', a: 0, why: 'Omit the tumtum: the baraita is about a hermaphrodite, which is a distinct entity.' },
        { ref: '42a:3', q: 'On the peace offering, "whether male or female" means a definite male or female, <span class="w">not a tumtum</span> or <span class="w">hermaphrodite</span>.', a: 0, why: 'Again: omit the tumtum.' },
        { ref: '42a:4', q: 'The second "male" for the sheep burnt offering excludes <span class="w">a tumtum</span> and <span class="w">a hermaphrodite</span>.', a: 0, why: 'Omit the tumtum from this baraita too.' },
        { ref: '42a:5-7', q: 'The first tanna on a bird killed by pinching: <span class="w">a tumtum</span> or <span class="w">hermaphrodite</span> bird is disqualified and imparts impurity in the throat. Rabbi Eliezer says it is fit, since birds are not written "male" and "female".', a: 0, why: 'Omit the tumtum: if it were just a male or female, why would the first tanna disqualify it?' },
        { ref: '42a:8-9', q: 'Rabbi Elazar: a tereifa, kilayim, a caesarean-born animal, <span class="w">a tumtum</span> and <span class="w">a hermaphrodite</span> do not become consecrated by substitution.', a: 0, why: 'Omit the tumtum. A doubtful animal would have to be consecrated, or at least make another one consecrated.' },
        { ref: '42a:11-12', q: 'Rabbi Shimon ben Yehuda: wherever the Torah says "male" it excludes <span class="w">a tumtum</span> and <span class="w">a hermaphrodite</span>. The Rabbis (first tanna): a hermaphrodite has no sanctity.', a: 2, why: 'Leave both. If you omit the tumtum, Rabbi Shimon ben Yehuda just agrees with the Rabbis, so there would be no dispute. The Gemara locates the dispute in the tumtum, then rejects that too (42b:1): everyone agrees a tumtum is doubtful, and they differ over the urination case in round 3.' }
      ];
      addMax(pen.length);
      pen.forEach(function (p, n) {
        var d = document.createElement('div');
        var q = document.createElement('p'); q.className = 'quote mb-2'; q.innerHTML = '<strong>' + (n + 1) + '.</strong> ' + p.q + ' ' + sef('Bekhorot ' + p.ref);
        var g = document.createElement('div'); g.className = 'grid gap-2 sm:grid-cols-3';
        var msg = document.createElement('p'); msg.className = 'mt-2 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]';
        d.appendChild(q); d.appendChild(g); d.appendChild(msg); $('pen').appendChild(d);
        mc(g, [{ t: 'Strike "tumtum"', ok: p.a === 0 }, { t: 'Strike "hermaphrodite"', ok: p.a === 1 }, { t: 'Leave both', ok: p.a === 2 }], function (ok) {
          if (ok) award();
          if (p.a === 0) Array.prototype.forEach.call(q.querySelectorAll('.w'), function (w, i) { if (w.textContent.indexOf('tumtum') > -1) w.classList.add('struck'); });
          msg.textContent = (ok ? 'Right. ' : 'Not quite. ') + p.why;
        });
      });

      // ROUND 2: five -> four
      var kinds = ['A tereifa', 'Kilayim (diverse kinds)', 'Caesarean-born', 'A tumtum', 'A hermaphrodite'];
      var struck = false;
      addMax(1);
      kinds.forEach(function (k, i) {
        var b = mkChip(k); b.id = 'k' + i;
        b.addEventListener('click', function () {
          if (struck) return;
          if (i !== 3) { $('fiveMsg').textContent = 'That one is on the Gemara\'s list as stated; only the tumtum is struck throughout this sugya.'; return; }
          struck = true; b.style.textDecoration = 'line-through'; b.style.opacity = '.5';
          $('fiveCount').textContent = '4 listed, but the baraita says five';
          $('fiveAsk').textContent = 'What does the Gemara slot in?';
          mc($('fiveFix'), [
            { t: 'An orphan: an animal born after its mother died', ok: true },
            { t: 'A firstborn', ok: false },
            { t: 'A blemished animal', ok: false }
          ], function (ok) {
            if (ok) { award(); $('fiveCount').textContent = '5 listed again'; }
            $('fiveMsg').innerHTML = (ok ? 'Right. ' : 'Not quite. ') + 'The Gemara says: remove the tumtum and bring in an orphan (yatom) in its place. ' + sef('Bekhorot 42a:10');
          });
        });
        $('five').appendChild(b);
      });

      // ROUND 3: urination
      var sp = 'A', pl = 'M', sg = 'R';
      function pr(a, b, v) { $(a).setAttribute('aria-pressed', v); $(b).setAttribute('aria-pressed', !v); }
      function urine() {
        pr('spA', 'spP', sp === 'A'); pr('plM', 'plF', pl === 'M'); pr('sgR', 'sgS', sg === 'R');
        $('strM').setAttribute('opacity', pl === 'M' ? 1 : 0); $('strF').setAttribute('opacity', pl === 'F' ? 1 : 0);
        var lamp, res, why;
        if (sp === 'P') { lamp = 'y'; res = 'Doubtful: male or female'; why = 'Reish Lakish: the Sages called a tumtum doubtful only for a person, whose male and female organs are in one concealed place. ' + sef('Bekhorot 42b:5'); }
        else if (pl === 'M') { lamp = 'g'; res = 'A male'; why = 'Everyone agrees that an animal urinating from the male place is a male. ' + sef('Bekhorot 42b:2'); }
        else if (sg === 'R') { lamp = 'y'; res = 'Doubtful'; why = 'The Rabbis are concerned that the male organ was turned round toward the female place. ' + sef('Bekhorot 42b:2'); }
        else { lamp = 'r'; res = 'A female: for a firstborn, non-sacred (ḥullin)'; why = 'Rabbi Shimon ben Yehuda is not concerned, and holds with Rabbi Elazar\'s ruling that such a firstborn is ḥullin. ' + sef('Bekhorot 42b:2'); }
        $('uLamp').className = 'lamp ' + lamp; $('uRes').textContent = res; $('uWhy').innerHTML = why;
      }
      $('spA').addEventListener('click', function () { sp = 'A'; urine(); });
      $('spP').addEventListener('click', function () { sp = 'P'; urine(); });
      $('plM').addEventListener('click', function () { pl = 'M'; urine(); });
      $('plF').addEventListener('click', function () { pl = 'F'; urine(); });
      $('sgR').addEventListener('click', function () { sg = 'R'; urine(); });
      $('sgS').addEventListener('click', function () { sg = 'S'; urine(); });
      urine();
      addMax(2);
      var chgBox = document.createElement('div'); chgBox.className = 'grid gap-2';
      $('chg').appendChild(chgBox);
      mc(chgBox, [
        { t: 'Rav Oshaya: perhaps its male organ turned round. Abaye: that is Rabbi Meir, who is concerned about the minority', ok: false },
        { t: 'Abaye bar Avin and Rav Ḥananya bar Avin: it already changed by being a tumtum, so maybe it changed in this too', ok: true }
      ], function (ok) {
        if (ok) award();
        var m = document.createElement('p'); m.className = 'mt-2 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]';
        m.innerHTML = 'Abaye answers Rav Oshaya with Rabbi Meir, but Abaye bar Avin and Rav Ḥananya bar Avin say the objection works even for the Rabbis: "since it changed, it changed" (hoil ve-ishtani ishtani), and the Sages dispute that principle. ' + sef('Bekhorot 42b:6-7');
        $('chg').appendChild(m);
      });
      var chg2 = document.createElement('div'); chg2.className = 'mt-3 grid gap-2';
      var q2 = document.createElement('p'); q2.className = 'mt-3 text-sm'; q2.textContent = 'Which Sage does the Gemara say follows Rabbi Elazar\'s ruling that a firstborn urinating from the female place is ḥullin?';
      $('chg').appendChild(q2); $('chg').appendChild(chg2);
      mc(chg2, [{ t: 'Rabbi Shimon ben Yehuda', ok: true }, { t: 'The Rabbis', ok: false }], function (ok) { if (ok) award(); });

      // ROUND 4: marriage
      var eli = true;
      function marryUpdate() {
        pr('eEl', 'eAk', eli);
        $('eLamp').className = 'lamp ' + (eli ? 'g' : 'r');
        $('eRule').textContent = eli ? 'Rabbi Eliezer: the wife of a naturally-born eunuch may enter levirate marriage.' : 'Rabbi Akiva: the wife of a naturally-born eunuch is not subject to levirate marriage; she is forbidden to his brothers.';
        $('eBar').textContent = eli ? 'the baraita where the tumtum\'s brother may do ḥalitza or yibum with his wife.' : 'the baraita where the wife of a tumtum does ḥalitza and not yibum.';
      }
      $('eEl').addEventListener('click', function () { eli = true; marryUpdate(); });
      $('eAk').addEventListener('click', function () { eli = false; marryUpdate(); });
      marryUpdate();
      var marry = [
        { q: 'A tumtum betroths a woman. The baraita says the betrothal is...', o: ['Not a betrothal', 'A betrothal, out of doubt: he may be a male'], a: 1, r: 'Bekhorot 42b:8' },
        { q: 'A tumtum\'s brother dies childless and there is no other brother. The widow...', o: ['Is exempt', 'Takes ḥalitza from the tumtum: he may be a male'], a: 1, r: 'Bekhorot 42b:9' },
        { q: 'Which tanna fits the baraita that a tumtum does not do ḥalitza even if other brothers exist, because he may be torn open and found a eunuch?', o: ['Rabbi Yehuda', 'Rabbi Yosei son of Rabbi Yehuda'], a: 1, r: 'Bekhorot 42b:14-16', n: 'Rabbi Yehuda says a torn-open tumtum found male is like a definite eunuch, so his widow would not even need ḥalitza. Rabbi Yosei son of Rabbi Yehuda says it is only a doubt.' },
        { q: 'Why does Rabbi Yosei son of Rabbi Yehuda say "perhaps" and not "he is a eunuch"?', o: ['Perhaps he is found female, or, if male, perhaps a naturally-born eunuch', 'Because every torn-open tumtum is found male'], a: 0, r: 'Bekhorot 42b:17-18' }
      ];
      addMax(marry.length);
      marry.forEach(function (m, n) {
        var d = document.createElement('div');
        var p = document.createElement('p'); p.className = 'mb-2 text-sm'; p.innerHTML = (n + 1) + '. ' + m.q + ' ' + sef(m.r);
        var g = document.createElement('div'); g.className = 'grid gap-2';
        var msg = document.createElement('p'); msg.className = 'mt-2 text-sm !text-[#adb2c7]';
        d.appendChild(p); d.appendChild(g); d.appendChild(msg); $('marry').appendChild(d);
        mc(g, m.o.map(function (t, i) { return { t: t, ok: i === m.a }; }), function (ok) { if (ok) award(); if (m.n) msg.textContent = m.n; });
      });
    })();
  </script>
</Layout>
